// The temperature control unit and the two stock parts it is built
// out of.
//
// One family of `tfs/assets/sprites.ron`'s roster. Every .ron in
// this directory is baked, in FILE-NAME order and then entry order,
// so the atlas layout is a function of the manifest and not of the
// filesystem. Two files claiming one sprite name is a bake error.
//
// GREYSCALE, AND THE COLOUR IS THE MACHINE'S WHOLE IDENTITY IN TG.
// The thermomachine is a GAGS object: `greyscale_config =
// /datum/greyscale_config/thermomachine` with `greyscale_colors =
// COLOR_VIBRANT_LIME` (thermomachine.dm:24-25), and its config
// (json_configs/thermomachine.json) is two layers per state -- a
// `temp_meter*` display that TAKES the colour, under a `thermo_base*`
// body that does not. That is exactly the shape `DmiBlend` bakes, so
// the pair is composited here with the meter painted and the body left
// alone, which is what `paint`'s per-layer flag is for.
//
// WHICH colour is the one thing that cannot be baked. tg recolours the
// machine live from its SETPOINT -- violet below 200 K through blue,
// cyan, lime, yellow and orange to red above 400
// (thermomachine.dm:98-117) -- and a baked atlas cell has one colour
// forever. So the art is baked at the colour a freshly built unit
// actually wears: its target ships at T20C, which falls in tg's
// `BODYTEMP_COLD_WARNING_1 to BODYTEMP_HEAT_WARNING_1` band, which is
// `COLOR_VIBRANT_LIME` (#00FF00). A unit dialled down to freezer
// temperatures stays lime here; the setpoint is on its panel instead.
//
// THE RUNNING LOOP IS NOT BAKED EITHER, and for the same reason from
// the other side: `thermo_base_1` and `temp_meter_1` are ten-frame
// rewinding loops, and `DmiBlend` composites one still. Baking the
// body's loop alone (`DmiAnim`) would drop the meter out of the
// running picture, so the running state is the loop's first frame --
// which is the frame with the indicator lit, so a running unit still
// reads as running from across the room. A blended ANIMATION source is
// the fix, and it is a baker feature rather than a manifest one.
(
    sheets: [
        ("thermomachine", "obj/machines/atmospherics/thermomachine.dmi"),
    ],
    sprites: [
        // The two positions. tg's `update_icon_state`
        // (thermomachine.dm:119-126) picks `thermo_base` for a unit
        // that is off or unpowered and `thermo_1` for `on &&
        // is_operational`, which is the same `working()` question this
        // engine's `positions` asks.
        //
        // `thermo-open` (the panel-open body) is deliberately absent:
        // this pack has no panel-open state on the machine, because
        // taking one apart is a crowbar against a switched-off unit
        // rather than tg's screwdriver-then-crowbar pair.
        ("thermo_off", DmiBlend(
            dmi: "@thermomachine",
            layers: [("temp_meter", Over, true), ("thermo_base", Over, false)],
            dir: 0,
            paint: (0, 255, 0),
        )),
        ("thermo_on", DmiBlend(
            dmi: "@thermomachine",
            layers: [("temp_meter_1", Over, true), ("thermo_base_1", Over, false)],
            dir: 0,
            paint: (0, 255, 0),
        )),
        // The stock parts this unit is built out of moved to
        // 72-stock-parts.ron the day they grew tiers: they are a family
        // of their own, and half of them are nothing to do with a
        // thermomachine.
    ],
)
